---
title: Example · sequence diagram
config:
  look: classic
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    actorBkg: "#333333"
    labelBoxBkgColor: "#fcd34d"
    labelTextColor: "#000000"
    noteTextColor: "#e0e0e0"
  themeCSS: |
    /* database · db */
    g.actor[transform] path { fill: #1c2f4a; stroke: #93c5fd; }
    /* queue */
    g.actor g[transform] path { fill: #2e2650; stroke: #c4b5fd; }
    /* database label clears the cylinder */
    g.actor[transform] + text { transform: translateY(12px); }
    g.actor[transform] + text tspan { paint-order: stroke; stroke: #1f1f1f; stroke-width: 6px; }
    /* collections · file */
    rect.actor:not([rx]) { fill: #3d3415; stroke: #fcd34d; }
  sequence:
    actorMargin: 80
    width: 200
    wrap: true
---
%% Behavior authority: <domain>.md.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User as developer
  box rgb(36, 36, 36) COA · system boundary
    participant Runtime as runtime<br/>call handling
    participant Worker as worker
  end
  participant DB@{ "type": "database", "alias": "state DB" }
  participant Queue@{ "type": "queue", "alias": "delivery queue" }
  participant Logs@{ "type": "collections", "alias": "native logs" }

  User->>+Runtime: task request
  Runtime->>Runtime: check input·permissions
  critical accept transaction
    Runtime->>DB: store operation
  option store failed
    Runtime-->>User: synchronous error
  end
  Runtime-)Worker: run notice · no wait for a reply
  Runtime-->>-User: accepted reply

  rect rgb(23, 61, 37)
    Note right of Worker: em · the span being explained
    loop until the final result
      par collect events
        Worker->>Logs: record run events
      and report status
        Worker->>DB: store progress
      end
    end
  end

  alt success
    Worker->>Queue: publish the result
    Queue--)User: asynchronous delivery
  else publish failed
    rect rgb(66, 35, 35)
      Worker-xQueue: publish rejected · issue
    end
  end

  opt cancel request
    User->>Runtime: cancel
    break already finished
      Runtime-->>User: existing final state
    end
  end

  Note over Runtime,DB: • a note spanning participants<br/>• one line per distinct statement
